# svc-naming: CP2's walk to the Sandgem lab, where Rowan offers a nickname
# for the starter: YES opens the naming screen (open_pokemon_naming_screen). The name is entered on the DS
# keyboard (cursor and A), a page switch, a delete, then typed text (as a physical keyboard does), and OK
# writes the nickname (the result var 0 takes the "nickname given" branch).
from opening.replay
+0 press down
until position 46 54
+0 release down
# east to Sandgem: the counterpart leads the way to the lab
until idle
+0 press b
+0 press down
until position 80 853
+0 release down
+0 press right
until position 104 853
+0 release right
+0 press up
until position 104 852
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 128 852 3600  # a wild battle on the way (seed 2) takes longer with longer battle texts
+0 release right
+0 press up
until position 128 848
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 136 848
+0 release right
+0 press up
until position 136 846
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 138 846
+0 release right
+0 press up
until position 138 845
+0 release up
+0 press right
until position 164 845
+0 release right
+0 release b
# lab: Rowan offers a nickname: YES
advance text 3300
until yesno
+0 press a
+1 release a
until app naming 600
+0 assert app naming
# The keyboard: A on "A" (row 0, col 0), right twice and A ("C"), the lower-case page by tap, "e" by tap.
+1 press a
+1 release a
+1 press right
+1 release right
+1 press right
+1 release right
+1 press a
+1 release a
+1 tap page:1
+1 tap key:0:4
+0 screenshot keyboard
# B deletes the "e"; then typed text
+1 press b
+1 release b
+1 tap type:ey
+1 tap ok
until app none
# "You're happy with the nickname?": YES; then Rowan gives the Pokédex
until yesno
+0 assert state party[0].nickname "ACey"
+0 press a
+1 release a
advance text 4000
until yesno
+0 press a
+1 release a
advance text 4500
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_HAS_POKEDEX true
